theory.intro:
A **unit fraction** has a numerator of $1$. Finding a unit fraction of a quantity means sharing the quantity into that many equal parts.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.9cm,every node/.style={font=\small}]
\fill[blue!25] (0,0) rectangle (1,1);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,1);
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,1);}
\node[above] at (0.5,1.05) {one part};
\draw[decorate,decoration={brace,mirror,amplitude=5pt}] (0,-0.15)--(5,-0.15);
\node[below] at (2.5,-0.35) {the whole quantity};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
